---
title: Crispy Seitan Bites
tags:
  - seitan
  - appetiser
---

-- ============ SEITAN ============

Add about an inch of water to a #pot with a #steamer basket{} and bring to a light boil.

In the meantime, whisk together @vital wheat gluten{111%g}, @all-purpose flour{30%g}, @vegetable broth powder{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1/2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1/2%tsp} and @salt{1/4%tsp} in a medium #bowl{}. Pour in @water{158%ml} and mix to form a ball of dough.

Lightly grease the steamer basket, then tear off bite-sized pieces of the seitan dough and place them in a single layer in the basket. Cover and steam for ~{10%minutes}.

-- ============ SAUCE (optional) ============
-- Original recipe notes suggest other sauce ideas; those notes weren't included in the source.

In the meantime, in a small #bowl{} or #measuring glass{}, mix together @Thai sweet chili sauce{44%ml}, @hoisin sauce{44%ml}, @soy sauce{30%ml}, @water{30%ml}, @rice vinegar{15%ml} and @sesame oil{1/2%tsp}. Set aside.

-- ============ COOK & FINISH ============

When the seitan is done steaming, heat @light oil{30%ml} [- canola or vegetable -] in a large #skillet{} or non-stick pan. -- 30 ml = the 2 tablespoons given in the method
Use #tongs{} to remove the seitan bites from the steamer basket and place them into the hot oil. Be careful as it may splatter. Cook a few minutes per side -- approx. ~{3%minutes} per side, source only says "a few minutes" -- until golden brown and crispy.

Remove from the heat, add the sauce and toss to coat. Garnish with @green onions{} or @chives{} [- small handful, chopped -] and @sesame seeds{1%tbsp} if desired, and serve hot.
